<h1>Search by course code</h1>
<p class="lead">
  Find study groups using a full or partial course code.
</p>

<h2>Before you begin</h2>
<p>
  <a href="/features/create-group">Create a group</a> for CS101
  if you want to follow the example below.
</p>

<h2>Step-by-step instructions</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Click <strong>Show all</strong> to clear previous filters.</li>
  <li>Click the <strong>Search code</strong> field.</li>
  <li>Type <strong>cs101</strong>. The list updates to show
      groups with matching course codes.</li>
  <li>Try <strong>CS</strong> to search using part of a course code.
      Search is case-insensitive, so uppercase and lowercase work.</li>
  <li>To search within a particular course, select it in the
      <strong>Course</strong> dropdown. Both filters apply together.</li>
  <li>Clear the search field to show all groups for the selected course,
      or click <strong>Show all</strong> to reset both filters.</li>
</ol>

<figure>
  <img src="/images/studyhub-search.png"
       alt="StudyHub showing CS101 Study Crew when lowercase cs101 is entered in Search code">
  <figcaption>
    Lowercase cs101 matches the CS101 course code.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<h2>If no results appear</h2>
<p>
  Check the course code and your selected course. For example,
  searching for CS101 while MATH101 is selected will not show
  a CS101 group. Click <strong>Show all</strong> and try again.
</p>

<aside class="notice">
  <strong>Search behavior:</strong>
  Leading and trailing spaces are ignored. Search matches course codes,
  not group names, descriptions, meeting times, or locations.
</aside>

<p>
  Next: <a href="/features/create-group">Create a group</a>
</p>

